 m.examples.push({title:'Four-resistor difference amplifier: topology is a prerequisite',detail:{problem:'An ideal matched-ratio difference stage has Rf/Rin=2, V2=1.1 V, V1=0.4 V. Find output and name its assumptions.',steps:['Confirm both resistor ratios are matched in the specific four-resistor difference topology.','Compute differential input V2−V1 = +0.7 V.','Multiply by 2 to obtain Vout=+1.4 V.','Require a valid common-mode range, negative feedback, appropriate output rails, bandwidth and loading.'],answer:'Ideal +1.4 V in the stated matched, linear circuit.',transfer:'Different resistor ratios can translate common-mode voltage into error; do not use the simplified equation for an arbitrary op-amp.'},sourceWeek:10});
